        <h2>
          You can name every product on that shelf. That was never the problem.
        </h2>
      

      
        <div class="lvg-truth-scorecard__two">

          
            <div>
              <p>Count what is on it. A cleanser. A serum for the breakouts. A second serum for the marks the breakouts left behind. Something you use twice a week and are slightly afraid of. A cream you bought because that thing stung. A moisturiser to sit over the cream. A sunscreen. Eleven steps on a good morning, four of them bought in the last six months.</p>
            </div>
          

          
            <div>
              <p>None of that came from carelessness. Every one of those products was bought for a reason, and the reason was good at the time. That is what makes the shelf so difficult to argue with — each purchase was rational, and the routine they add up to is not.</p><p>You did not build this. You were handed it, one reasonable purchase at a time.</p>
            </div>
          

        </div>
      

    </article>
